$1\,\mathrm{kpc}$ â the galaxy core scale. The framework predicts spatial flatness
$\Omega_{\rm total} = 1$ and a scale-duality relation
$M\,\mdelta = (\sqrt{8}/8\pi)\,\mP^2$
connecting macroscopic baryonic mass to ultralight dark matter mass.
The same $C_3$ geometry determines the cosmic energy budget exactly. The CMB
octupole-to-quadrupole power ratio derived from the three-defect horizon equals the
dark-energy-to-dark-matter density ratio: $\Omega_\Lambda/\Omega_c = C_3/C_2 = 5/2$.
Combined with the baryon fraction $\Omega_b/\Omega_c = \alpha_{\rm TRSD}\,n =
\sqrt{3}/(3\pi)$ and spatial flatness, this yields
$\Omega_b \approx 4.99\%$, $\Omega_c \approx 27.15\%$, $\Omega_\Lambda \approx 67.87\%$
