$S_{\rm EH} = (c^4/16\pi G)\tau\int R\sqrt{g}\,d^2x = c^4\delta\tau/(8\pi G)$.
The physical source is a cosmic string with string tension $T$ (energy per unit
length). The point-source action on a reference length $L_{\rm ref}$ is
$S_T = -T\,L_{\rm ref}\,c\,\tau$. Action stationarity gives the
\emph{string-tension deficit-angle relation}:
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{\delta = \frac{8\pi G}{c^4}\,T,\qquad T = \frac{Mc^2}{L_{\rm ref}}.}
  \label{eq:mass_defect}
\end{equation}
For the cosmic context $L_{\rm ref} = R_H = c/H_0$, so $T = Mc^2 H_0/c = McH_0$.
