The inverse gives $H_0 = \az/(\atrsd c)$. This bridges the galactic acceleration
scale to the cosmic expansion rate through a pure number derived from $C_3$ horizon
geometry. Since every derived quantity scales uniformly with $H_0$, the framework
does not fix $H_0$ absolutely; an additional quantization condition (e.g., fixing
the horizon area in Planck units) is required for an absolute prediction of $H_0$.

\subsection{Information-Energy Equivalence}
\label{subsec:info_energy}

The defect normalization map gives the mass-defect relation
\begin{equation}
\delta = \frac{8\pi G M}{c^2 R_H}.
\label{eq:mass_defect_info}
\end{equation}
Using the total horizon information
\begin{equation}
I = \frac{\delta}{2\pi}\, N,
\label{eq:I_defect}
\end{equation}
where $N = A_{\rm eff}/\ell_P^2$ is the number of Planck cells on the
defect-modified horizon with $A_{\rm eff} = 2\pi R_H^2$ and
$\ell_P^2 = \hbar G/c^3$, we eliminate $\delta$.
Using the corrected defect map $\delta = 8\pi GM/(c^2 R_H)$, which gives
$Mc^2 = \delta c^4 R_H/(8\pi G)$ (i.e.\ $f_\delta^2 = Mc^2/R_H$):
\[
  E = Mc^2 = \frac{\delta c^4 R_H}{8\pi G}
  = \frac{c^4 R_H}{8\pi G}\cdot\frac{2\pi I}{N}
  = \frac{c^4 R_H}{4G}\cdot\frac{I\,\ell_P^2}{A_{\rm eff}}
  = \frac{c^4 R_H}{4G}\cdot\frac{\hbar G}{c^3}\cdot\frac{I}{2\pi R_H^2}.
\]
Simplifying:
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
E = Mc^2 = \frac{\hbar c}{8\pi R_H}\, I .
}
\label{eq:info_energy_equiv}
\end{equation}
This states that energy, mass, and information are the same physical quantity
measured in different units. The factor $\hbar c/(8\pi R_H)$ is the energy per
bit of horizon information, consistent with $I$ counting Planck-area cells on
the horizon. The factor is linear in $R_H$, as the defect map
$\delta = 8\pi GM/(c^2R_H)$ requires. Dark energy is then the information energy of the total
horizon defect,
\begin{equation}
\rho_{\rm DE}
= \frac{E_{\mathcal I}}{V}
= \frac{\hbar c}{R_H}\cdot\frac{I}{V}
= \frac{1}{\delta_{\rm gen}}\frac{f_\pi^2}{R_H^2},
\end{equation}
exactly as derived earlier. No new substance is required.

\noindent\textbf{Physical interpretation.}
Mass is a conical defect angle. Energy is the work required to create that
defect. Information is the number of Planck cells on the boundary of that
defect. The identity \eqref{eq:info_energy_equiv} replaces $E=mc^2$ with a
geometric-informational equality. In this picture, dark energy is not a new
fluid; it is the lost information of energy, encoded on the horizon and
driving accelerated expansion.

