\subsection{Horizon Boundary Condition and Null Propagation}
\label{subsec:horizon_boundary_final}

The cosmic horizon at the terminal state is a null hypersurface carrying the
total conical deficit $\delta_{\rm total} = \pi$. We impose the boundary
condition that the energy-momentum tensor of the massless scalar field
satisfies the null energy condition with equality:
\begin{equation}
g^{\mu\nu}\partial_\mu\chi\,\partial_\nu\chi \to 0
\quad\text{on the boundary}.
\label{eq:null_condition_final}
